      "lv2spells": [
        {
          "name": "Speak with Animals (Constant)",
          "type": "spell",
          "level": 2,
          "traits": [
            "concentrate"
          ],
          "castingTime": "2",
          "duration": "10 minutes",
          "range": "",
          "area": "",
          "targets": "",
          "save": "",
          "description": "<p>You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. The spell doesn't make them more friendly than normal. Cunning animals are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.</p>",
          "cast": false,
          "cost": "",
          "primaryCheck": "",
          "secondaryCasters": "",
          "secondaryChecks": "",
          "id": "D6Xun7rk5Brir0IF"
        }
      ],
      "lv3spells": [
        {
          "name": "Animal Vision (At Will) (Dinosaurs Only)",
          "type": "spell",
          "level": 3,
          "traits": [
            "concentrate",
            "manipulate"
          ],
          "castingTime": "1 minute",
          "duration": "1 hour",
          "range": "120 feet",
          "area": "",
          "targets": "1 animal",
          "save": "",
          "description": "<p>You tap into the target's senses, allowing you to see, hear, and otherwise sense whatever it senses for the spell's duration. If the target wishes to prevent you from doing so, it can attempt a Will save, negating the spell on a success, but most animals don't bother to do so. While tapping into the target's senses, you can't use your own body's senses, but you can change back and forth from your body's senses to the target's senses using a single action, which has the concentrate trait.</p>",
          "cast": false,
          "cost": "",
          "primaryCheck": "",
          "secondaryCasters": "",
          "secondaryChecks": "",
          "id": "UOtcq8C7cvf4ZBlr"
        }
      ],
